-- Migration 29: Versioning seed fields for transformation results.
--
-- Re-running a transformation on a source that already has a result from it
-- never overwrote anything - create_insight_command (commands/
-- embedding_commands.py) always CREATEs a new source_insight row, it never
-- UPDATEs one. What was missing was a coherent "version" concept to present
-- that history (today it's a flat, growing list of same-titled insights).
--
-- This migration only adds two optional, purely additive fields so a future
-- write path can record them explicitly:
--   * transformation: which transformation produced this insight (today the
--     only link is the fragile insight_type == transformation.title match).
--   * version: an explicit 1-based version number for this
--     (source, transformation) pair.
-- Both are optional with no default and no backfill: existing (and, until a
-- write path sets them, new) rows simply have version = NONE, and callers
-- treat that as "implicitly version 1" ordered by created - see
-- Transformation.get_result_versions() in open_notebook/domain/
-- transformation.py, which computes version history today from existing
-- data and prefers an explicit `version` value once something populates it.
-- No data loss, no backfill required.

DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS transformation ON TABLE source_insight TYPE option<record<transformation>>;
DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS version ON TABLE source_insight TYPE option<int>;
